# 009 — /vendor/products/:id asserts the tenant boundary.
#
# GET had only query validation, POST only body+query, DELETE `middlewares: []`.
# The sole boundary was `policies: [...]`, which is inert whenever the `rbac`
# feature flag is off — its default. Ownership is a tenant boundary, not a
# permission, so it must not share that kill switch: POST, DELETE and
# `/cancel` now run an always-on middleware over the existing
# `ensureSellerOwnsProduct` helper (NOT_FOUND, never FORBIDDEN).
#
# GET is different on purpose: `applySellerProductLinkFilter` deliberately shows
# the shared master catalogue, so blanket-404 would break offer creation. The
# visibility predicate is extracted once and used by both list and detail, so
# the detail route shows exactly what the list shows — another seller's DRAFT
# (the actual leak) 404s, a PUBLISHED catalogue product still 200s.
#
# The `policies: [...]` declarations are left untouched: they are the RBAC layer
# and become meaningful when the flag is on.

